            "vuln_file": "fs/hfs/mdb.c",
            "stmt_text": "\tHFS_SB(sb)->bitmap = kzalloc(8192, GFP_KERNEL);",
            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This statement allocates a fixed 8192-byte buffer for the bitmap without validating the actual filesystem block count (fs_ablocks). If fs_ablocks is maliciously crafted to exceed what fits in 8192 bytes, subsequent reads into this buffer will cause a buffer overflow, as noted in the relevance=0.90 analysis."
          },
          {
            "vuln_file": "fs/hfs/mdb.c",
            "stmt_text": "\twhile (size) {",
            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This while loop processes the bitmap data without explicit bounds validation against the allocated 8192-byte buffer. Combined with the unvalidated size calculation from fs_ablocks, this creates a path for out-of-bounds memory access when processing malicious filesystem metadata."
          },
          {
            "vuln_file": "fs/hfs/mdb.c",
            "stmt_text": "\tsize = min(HFS_SB(sb)->alloc_blksz, (u32)PAGE_SIZE);",
            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This allocation block size calculation lacks sufficient validation of the raw value from the Master Directory Block. Insufficient validation of alloc_blksz could allow integer overflow or improper size calculations that propagate through subsequent bitmap operations."
          }
        ]
